": ["non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer"]}, "processing_info": {"total_entities_found": 84, "total_relations_found": 198, "entities_after_truncation": 10, "relations_after_truncation": 30, "merged_chunks_count": 36, "final_chunks_count": 1}}, "question": "Which treatments are used for non–muscle-invasive bladder cancer and what surgical procedure is typically involved?", "question_type": "Complex Reasoning", "ground_truth": "TURBT and intravesical therapy (BCG or chemotherapy) are used for non–muscle-invasive bladder cancer.", "evidence": "TURBT is used for non–muscle-invasive bladder cancer.; Intravesical therapy is used for non–muscle-invasive bladder cancer.; BCG is a type of intravesical therapy for non–muscle-invasive bladder cancer.; Chemotherapy is a type of intravesical therapy for non–muscle-invasive bladder cancer.", "evidence_relations": "Stage 0 and Stage 1 bladder cancers are non–muscle-invasive; TURBT is used for tumor removal in non–muscle-invasive bladder cancer; Intravesical therapy (BCG or chemotherapy) is used for non–muscle-invasive bladder cancer", "split": "train", "error": null}
